  {
   "id": "examples-imports-md-5",
   "kind": {
    "type": "markdown"
   },
   "source": "## `use @lang`\n\n`use @lang <language> \"<module>\" as <alias>` declares a module for a polyglot\nblock. It is accepted and runs, but the alias is not wired to the block's\nvariables — the block still has to `import` the module itself:\n",
   "state": {
    "status": "done"
   },
   "meta": {},
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "id": "examples-imports-4",
   "kind": {
    "type": "crush"
   },
   "source": "use @lang python \"math\" as math\n\n@python {\nimport math\nv = math.factorial(5)\n}\nprint(v)\n",
   "state": {
    "status": "pending"
   },
